---
import Layout from '../layout.astro';
import TaxQuestion from '../components/TaxQuestion.astro';
const qs=['Do I have enough money to retire well?','How much can I comfortably spend in retirement?','How should I create income from my investments?','How much cash should I keep in retirement?','Should I roll my 401(k) into an IRA?','Should I do Roth conversions before RMDs?','Which accounts should I withdraw from first?','How should I invest differently once I retire?','How can I give more efficiently in retirement?','How much can I give my kids without hurting my retirement?'];
---
<Layout title="Retirement Planning | RIPL Wealth" description="Retirement planning for successful people who want to understand not only whether they can retire, but how well.">
<section class="hero"><div class="wrap"><div class="eyebrow">RETIREMENT</div><h1>You've built enough to retire. Now let's see how well you can retire.</h1><p class="small">By RIPL Wealth · Updated September 30, 2026</p><p class="lead">The question isn't only whether your money will last. It's what your wealth can make possible once work becomes optional.</p></div></section>
<section class="section"><div class="wrap article"><h2>There's a difference between retiring and retiring well.</h2><p>For many successful people, retirement isn't a question of whether they can stop working. They can.</p><p>The more interesting question is what happens next.</p><p>Can you spend more confidently? Travel more? Help your kids while you're here to see the impact? Give more to the organizations and causes you care about? Leave more behind?</p><div class="callout"><h3>Better planning isn't only about what you get to keep.</h3><p>It's about what your wealth allows you to do.</p></div></div></section>
<section class="section dark"><div class="wrap"><h2>Retirement changes the job of your money.</h2><p class="lead">While you were building wealth, much of your money had one primary assignment: grow. Retirement changes that.</p><div class="retirement-jobs"><span>SPEND</span><span>INCOME</span><span>GROW</span><span>GIVE</span><span>LEGACY</span></div><p>Some money needs to provide income. Some needs to stay available. Some may need to continue growing for decades. And some may ultimately be used to help your family, support causes you care about or leave a legacy.</p><p class="answer"><strong>The goal isn't to make every dollar do the same thing. It's to give every dollar the right job.</strong></p></div></section>
<TaxQuestion context="retirement"/>
<section class="section questions"><div class="wrap"><div class="eyebrow">RETIREMENT MONEY QUESTIONS</div><h2>What are you trying to figure out?</h2><div class="grid">{qs.map((q,i)=><a class="card" href="/money-questions/"><span class="num">{String(i+1).padStart(2,'0')}</span><h3>{q}</h3></a>)}</div></div></section>
<section class="final-cta"><div class="wrap"><h2>The question may not be whether you can retire. The better question is how well you can retire.</h2><p>Let's understand what the wealth you've built can reasonably make possible.</p><a class="btn" href="/contact/">Let's Talk Through It </a></div></section>
</Layout>